 183: ## 4. Normative locks (L1╞Æ?"L13)
 184: 
 185: | ID | Lock |
 186: |----|------|
 187: | **L1** | **Claims-with-evidence.** Affirmative public claims for a release must appear on the claims checklist with an evidence pointer (doc path, test name, report hash, residual ID, or review disposition). |
 188: | **L2** | **Forbidden claims.** No SOC2/ISO/GDPR/ASVS-Level certification; no perfect deletion / NIST Purge-Destroy as product property; no metadata-private sync; no third-party plugin sandbox / WASI marketplace; no inventing doctor/recovery-export CLIs; no ╞Æ?ofull DB encryption╞Æ?? without F8 qualifier; no UI grants authority beyond contracts; no ╞Æ?oSSDF/OpenSSF fully compliant.╞Æ?? |
 189: | **L3** | **Residual citation (full cross-walk).** RELEASE-CLAIMS must disposition **every open row** in T184 `residuals.md` (cite R-ID **or** explicit ╞Æ?oout of scope for claims╞Æ??). **Minimum cite set** (user-trust floor): R-F8, R-CE-PRE, R-ACK, R-META, R-TB, R-API-VER, R-12, R-34.2, **R-CI-SAST, R-CI-BRANCH, R-AUDIT-UNMAINT, R-PIPE-IU, R-UDS-TMP, R-ZERO-KEY, R-DESKTOP-OPEN, R-SLSA, R-DOC-CLI**. R-ZERO-KEY + F8 must co-qualify any ╞Æ?oencrypted vault╞Æ?? language. |
 190: | **L4** | **Hard SCA gate.** `cargo deny check` and `cargo audit` (exit code only, F27) **must** pass on the release commit. Unmaintained warnings (R-AUDIT-UNMAINT) do not fail audit by themselves under current policy; document delta if policy tightens. |
 191: | **L5** | **SBOM required for binary distribution.** CycloneDX JSON via **`cargo-cyclonedx`** with **`--spec-version 1.5`**, **`--describe binaries`**, and **target/features matching the release build**. One BOM per shipped binary. Source-only tags may attach SBOM as soft. |
 192: | **L6** | **NOTICE for binary ship.** Binary distribution includes machine-generated third-party license text (`cargo-about` preferred; committed `about.toml` + template). Source-only may omit if LICENSE + deny policy cover. |
 193: | **L7** | **Tool licenses.** Release-gate tools must be MIT/Apache/BSD/ISC (or already-allowed deny licenses). **No AGPL/GPL required tooling.** |
 194: | **L8** | **Platform smoke match.** Claims of T1 support require smoke evidence whose **runner label** matches COMPATIBILITY tiers (Windows `windows-2025`, Linux `ubuntu-24.04`; macOS only as documented soft pin). |
 195: | **L9** | **SLSA honesty.** Do not claim SLSA Build L3 or ╞Æ?ocertified SLSA╞Æ?? without isolated provenance + documented `builder.id`. Optional L1-oriented attestations only when fields present **and** repo/plan supports attestations (public or Enterprise Cloud private). |
 196: | **L10** | **No packaging DoD.** MSI, notarization, App Store, systemd/launchd production units are **out of scope** for T185 completion (documented residual). |
 197: | **L11** | **Human claims sign-off.** Checklist includes a human owner field; agent automation may prepare evidence but does not alone clear L1. |
 198: | **L12** | **No force-push / no main direct release.** Release tags from agreed branch; follow `AGENTS.md` Git rules. Dry-run RC does not require a public tag if user prefers private evidence only. Note R-CI-BRANCH: branch protection may be **unenforced** until repo admin enables it ╞Æ?" do not claim enforced protection. |
 199: | **L13** | **Automated non-claims scan.** Release gate runs a scripted forbidden-phrase check over elevated docs (`scripts/check-release-claims.ps1`); fails on affirmative overclaims. Complements (does not replace) human checklist review. |
